From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:48:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: coda: add CODA980 H.264 encoder for the Sophgo SG2000

The Sophgo SG2000 has a Chips&Media CODA980 for H.264. The CODA980 has
the CODA960 command interface, with these differences:

- frame memory control: BWB in bit 15, 128-bit little endian frames
- SPS header: the host gives the level
- PPS header: the host sets CABAC and 8x8 transform off
- rate control takes other parameters
- no subsampled reference frames
- one frame cache configuration register

Support the H.264 encoder only, at constant QP. The SG2000 also needs its
codec control block, to give the shared SRAM to the H.264 core, and three
bus and source clocks. Run without the SRAM for now.

The register sequence follows Sophgo's vendor driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
